d the labels distinct, one per item. Its steps are checkout, `rustup toolchain install` and install-action with `cargo-nextest@0.9.146,cargo-mutants@27.1.0`, then one `shell: pwsh` step that reads `PACKAGE` / `FILES` from step `env:` and runs `scripts/agent-run.ps1 run --mutants --package <member> --file …`. It has no cache, upload, secret, `concurrency:` or `needs:`. Its job log, the harness document plus cargo-mutants' outcome lines, is the audit's read, and the harness document judges a job. The harness leaves a missed mutant the Windows build never compiled (a `#[cfg(unix)]` twin in a scoped file) out of the count and names it in the document's `mutants.host_excluded` (test-plan §3 `run` step 4), while cargo-mutants' own lines still say MISSED for it. Run 38036448183 read all nine jobs green with 30 mutants left out, as measured at `viola-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-windows-mutation-grade/evidence/windows-dispatch.md`. No workflow has a `concurrency:` block. zizmor's pedantic `concurrency-limits` was declined because a concurrency group cancels pending runs, which would drop a cancelled run's `always()` gate and upload chain. (No push or pull-request run carries a mutation job — mutation testing moved to the epoch-boundary code audit on 2026-09-28, and `windows-mutants.yml` uploads nothing — so a cancelled run cannot lose mutation coverage; that half of the original reason is retired.)
